d applications, and handling contradictory or incomplete supervision data. Overton automates the life cycle of model construction, deployment, and monitoring by providing a set of novel high-level, declarative abstractions. Overton's vision is to shift developers to these higher-level tasks instead of lower-level machine learning tasks. In fact, using Overton, engineers can build deep-learning-based applications without writing any code in frameworks like TensorFlow. For over a year, Overton has been used in production to support multiple applications in both near-real-time applications and back-of-house processing. In that time, Overton-based applications have answered billions of queries in multiple languages and processed trillions of records reducing errors 1.7-2.9 times versus production systems."}], "license": "mit"}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 4, "tags": ["transformers", "pytorch", "t5", "text2text-generation", "dataset:arxiv", "license:mit", "text-generation-inference", "endpoints_compatible", "region:us"], "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2022-06-17T04:46:15.000Z", "modelId": "Suva/uptag-url-model-v2"}, {"_id": "68f4918a46fd5384a8c31d02", "id": "ubitech-edg/mistral-12b-cpt", "cardData": {"language": ["en"], "license": "apache-2.0", "tags": ["text-generation", "causal-lm", "continual-pretraining", "lora", "axolotl", "deepspeed", "transformers", "mistral", "nemo", "eu-hpc"], "datasets": ["arxiv", "gov", "news", "wikipedia"], "metrics": ["loss"], "library_name": "transformers", "framework": "pytorch", "base_model": "mistralai/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407", "model_name": "mistral-12b-cpt", "pipeline_tag": "text-generation", "task_categories": ["text-generation"], "model_type": "AutoModelForCausalLM", "inference": {"parameters": {"max_new_tokens": 512, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9}}, "trained_on": ["Leonardo EuroHPC"], "description": "Continual pretraining (CPT) of Mistral 12B Nemo Instruct using Axolotl and DeepSpeed ZeRO-1. Trained on scientific, government, news, and Wikipedia text with LoRA adapters."}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 4, "tags": ["transformers", "safetensors", "mistral", "text-generation", "causal-lm", "continual-pretraining", "lora", "axolotl", "deepspeed", "nemo", "eu-hpc", "conversational", "en", "dataset:arxiv", "dataset:gov", "dataset:news", "dataset:wikipedia", "base_model:mistralai/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407", "base_model:adapter:mistralai/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407", "license:apache-2.0", "text-generation-inference", "endpoints_compatible", "region:us"], "pipeline_tag": "text-generation", "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2025-10-19T07:21:46.000Z", "modelId": "ubitech-edg/mistral-12b-cpt"}, {"_id": "68fb9fd79f5b54bba1a46864", "id": "ubitech-edg/qwen2.5-72b-cpt", "cardData": {"language": ["en"], "license": "apache-2.0", "tags": ["text-generation", "causal-lm", "continual-pretraining", "lora", "axolotl", "deepspeed", "transformers", "qwen", "llava", "eu-hpc"], "datasets": ["arxiv", "gov", "news", "wikipedia"], "metrics": ["loss"], "library_name": "transformers", "framework": "pytorch", "base_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B", "model_name": "qwen2.5-72b-cpt", "pipeline_tag": "text-generation", "task_categories": ["text-generation"], "model_type": "AutoModelForCausalLM", "inference": {"parameters": {"max_new_tokens": 512, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9}}, "trained_on": ["Leonardo EuroHPC"], "description": "Continual pretraining (CPT) of Qwen2.5-72B using Axolotl and DeepSpeed ZeRO-1. The model was trained with 4-bit NF4 LoRA adapters on scientific, governmental, news, and Wikipedia text corpora to improve factual grounding, reasoning, and domain coverage in the energy and governance sectors. This repository hosts LoRA adapters only, designed to be loaded on top of Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B."}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 4, "tags": ["transformers", "safetensors", "qwen2", "text-generation", "causal-lm", "continual-pretraining", "lora", "axolotl", "deepspeed", "qwen", "llava", "eu-hpc", "conversational", "en", "dataset:arxiv", "dataset:gov", "dataset:news", "dataset:wikipedia", "base_model:Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B", "base_model:adapter:Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B", "license:apache-2.0", "text-generation-inference", "endpoints_compatible", "4-bit", "bitsandbytes", "region:us"], "pipeline_tag": "text-generation", "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2025-10-24T15:48:39.000Z", "modelId": "ubitech-edg/qwen2.5-72b-cpt"}, {"_id": "69463f02631967076994112c", "id": "Tasfiya025/AcademicAbstractGenerator", "cardData": {"tags": ["text-generation", "gpt2", "language-modeling", "academic"], "library_name": "transformers", "license": "mit", "datasets": ["arxiv"], "metrics": ["perplexity"]}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 4, "tags": ["transformers", "gpt2", "text-generation", "language-modeling", "academic", "dataset:arxiv", "license:mit", "endpoints_compatible", "region:us"], "pipeline_tag": "text-generation", "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2025-12-20T06:15:30.000Z", "modelId": "Tasfiya025/AcademicAbstractGenerator"}, {"_id": "621ffdc136468d709f177744", "id": "Suva/uptag-url-model", "cardData": {"datasets": ["arxiv"], "widget": [{"text": "summarize: We describe a system called Overton, whose main design goal is to support engineers in building, monitoring, and improving production machinelearning systems. Key challenges engineers face are monitoring fine-grained quality, diagnosing errors in sophisticated applications, and handling contradictory or incomplete supervision data. Overton automates the life cycle of model construction, deployment, and monitoring by providing a set of novel high-level, declarative abstractions. Overton's vision is to shift developers to these higher-level tasks instead of lower-level machine learning tasks. In fact, using Overton, engineers can build deep-learning-based applications without writing any code in frameworks like TensorFlow. For over a year, Overton has been used in production to support multiple applications in both near-real-time applications and back-of-house processing. In that time, Overton-based applications have answered billions of queries in multiple languages and processed trillions of records reducing errors 1.7-2.9 times versus production systems."}], "license": "mit"}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 3, "tags": ["transformers", "pytorch", "t5", "text2text-generation", "dataset:arxiv", "license:mit", "text-generation-inference", "endpoints_compatible", "region:us"], "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2022-03-02T23:29:05.000Z", "modelId": "Suva/uptag-url-model"}, {"_id": "6417c46db0c64fa25a126053", "id": "cloudqi/cqi_brain_memory_summarizer_oneline_pt_v0", "cardData": {"datasets": ["arxiv"], "widget": [{"text": "summarize: We describe a system called Overton, whose main design goal is to support engineers in building, monitoring, and improving production machinelearning systems. Key challenges engineers face are monitoring fine-grained quality, diagnosing errors in sophisticated applications, and handling contradictory or incomplete supervision data. Overton automates the life cycle of model construction, deployment, and monitoring by providing a set of novel high-level, declarative abstractions. Overton's vision is to shift developers to these higher-level tasks instead of lower-level machine learning tasks. In fact, using Overton, engineers can build deep-learning-based applications without writing any code in frameworks like TensorFlow. For over a year, Overton has been used in production to support multiple applications in both near-real-time applications and back-of-house processing. In that time, Overton-based applications have answered billions of queries in multiple languages and processed trillions of records reducing errors 1.7-2.9 times versus production systems."}], "license": "mit"}, "likes": 1, "private": false, "downloads": 3, "tags": ["transformers", "pytorch", "t5", "text2t